# Cursor AI Rules for RedLine Souls Server

## 📖 Primary Reference
**ALWAYS read `CLAUDE.md` first** - Complete technical documentation for AI assistants working on this project.

## 🚫 Critical Constraints
- User is `acserver` (NOT root) - no sudo access
- Never suggest `sudo` commands or system package installs
- Use `pip3 install --user` if Python packages needed (but prefer built-in modules)
- Never commit: `.env`, `cfg/server_cfg.ini`, `logs/`, `player_stats.json`

## ✅ Always Do
- Check `CLAUDE.md` for architectural context before suggesting changes
- Use environment variables from `.env` (never hardcode credentials)
- Add `?wait=true` to Discord webhook POST requests (required for message editing)
- Restart server (`./stop_server.sh && ./start_server.sh`) after AI traffic changes
- Restart systemd service after unified_announcer.py changes: `systemctl --user restart unified-announcer.service`
- Provide test commands with any change suggestions
- Keep README.md user-friendly (technical details → CLAUDE.md)

## 🎯 Code Patterns
- Environment loading: Custom fallback parser (no python-dotenv)
- Log monitoring: Seek/tell position tracking pattern
- Discord editing: Store message_id from POST, PATCH to edit later
- Error handling: Try/except with traceback, auto-recovery where possible

## 📂 File Structure
- Root: Main scripts, shell scripts
- `cfg/`: Server configuration (extra_cfg.yml = AI traffic/weather)
- `_docs/`: Human documentation
- `_utils/`: Utility scripts
- `logs/`: Server logs (gitignored)
- `.env`: Secrets (gitignored, use `.env.example` as template)

## 🔧 Common Tasks
- AI traffic → `cfg/extra_cfg.yml` → restart server
- Discord → `unified_announcer.py` → restart systemd service
- Stats → `player_stats.py` → kill old process, restart manually
- Logs → `./archive_old_logs.sh` (keeps 7 days, gzip compresses old)

## 🧠 Context Files
1. `CLAUDE.md` - Technical deep-dive (read first!)
2. `README.md` - User docs (keep friendly)
3. `.env.example` - Environment variable template
4. `cfg/extra_cfg.yml` - Server configuration

Full details in CLAUDE.md - this is just a quick reference!
